      "message": "We could set this only once, but still need to Link/Unlink based on `pushConstantRangeCount \u003d\u003d 0`.\n\nHere the state I\u0027m pretty sure makes the logic fall over in some cases. So at init we\u0027d do:\n\n```\n mCachedCreateInfo.pushConstantRange.stageFlags \u003d\n            VK_SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT_BIT | VK_SHADER_STAGE_COMPUTE_BIT | VK_SHADER_STAGE_VERTEX_BIT;\n        mCachedCreateInfo.pushConstantRange.offset \u003d 0;\n```\n\nThen here:\n\n```\nif (immediateDataSize \u003d\u003d 0) {\n  mCachedCreateInfo.layout.pPushConstantRanges \u003d nullptr;\n} else {\n  mCachedCreateInfo.pushConstantRange.size \u003d internalImmediateDataSize;\n  mCachedCreateInfo.layout.pPushConstantRanges \u003d \u0026mCachedCreateInfo.pushConstantRange;\n}\n```\n\nAlthough now I have a concern about that cache for future multithreading. I guess we\u0027ll see about it then.",
